<article class="env-lemma" id="08MR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08MR">Lemma <span data-tag="08MR">91.11.4</span>.</a> Let $(f, f')$ be a morphism of first order thickenings as in Situation <a href="/tag/08M7" data-tag="08M7">91.9.1</a>. Let $\mathcal{F}'$, $\mathcal{G}'$ be $\mathcal{O}'$-modules and set $\mathcal{F} = i^*\mathcal{F}'$ and $\mathcal{G} = i^*\mathcal{G}'$. Let $\varphi : \mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{G}$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-linear map. Assume that $\mathcal{G}'$ is flat over $\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{B}'}$ and that $(f, f')$ is a strict morphism of thickenings. The set of lifts of $\varphi $ to an $\mathcal{O}'$-linear map $\varphi ' : \mathcal{F}' \to \mathcal{G}'$ is, if nonempty, a principal homogeneous space under </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _\mathcal {O}(\mathcal{F}, \mathcal{G} \otimes _\mathcal {O} f^*\mathcal{J})  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Lemmas <a href="/tag/08MP" data-tag="08MP">91.11.1</a> and <a href="/tag/08MQ" data-tag="08MQ">91.11.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>